Some of the Company’s customers are located in emerging markets, which can further exacerbate the foregoing risks.

Russia’s invasion of Ukraine on February 24, 2022, and its resulting impacts, including supply chain disruptions, increased fuel prices, international sanctions and other measures that have been imposed, have adversely affected, and may continue to adversely affect, the Company’s business and services, including our employees from or located in Ukraine. These factors may exacerbate other risks to the Company’s business, any of which could materially and adversely affect the business and results of operations.

